					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/vaelynx" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(914331); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=914331&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608930980" alt="VAElynx" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=914331)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/vaelynx" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(914331); return false;" >VAElynx</a></span> <span class="odate time_1319495708 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">24 Oct 2011 22:35</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1289450">
									

<p>Okay&#8230; this might be because I don't know the two characters, (which is why I aren't downvoting) but going against that many (some of them probably armed) church members in melee seems slightly above human forces.<br />
Especially since, although panic is a powerful tool, most of them had nowhere to go and such people get reckless. The reason why that worked for Clef's <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Kitsune</span>SCP-953 is because of her being able to cause hallucinations.<br />
I like what she did, though seems to me like a more foundation-like thing would be to pump the place with nerve gas, then mess with evidence to make it seem like a mass suicide.</p>

							</div>

								
					
