		<div class="post" id="post-1289459">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,1289459)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-1289459">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-gears" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(172464); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=172464&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608930980" alt="Dr Gears" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=172464)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-gears" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(172464); return false;" >Dr Gears</a></span> <span class="odate time_1319496439 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">24 Oct 2011 22:47</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1289459">
									

<p>I think that confusion is partially my fault. Kramer is, at this point, only partially organic anymore. Because of multiple experiments, <a href="/scp-212">SCP-212</a> exposure, and other rubbish, she's well above average human capabilities. She has a lot of &quot;built in&quot; equipment and weapons, and has enormous control of her biological processes, like heart rate, synapse response, and other things that let her, temporally, fight like the hand of Death itself.</p>
<p>That being said, it's not something that happens a lot. She's at the point where she's not sure if she's actually a human being anymore. She's very bipolar, prone to bouts of depression, total emotional withdrawal, and a host of other mental disorders, both from her screwed-up life and due to physical alterations and damage to her brain. She's the muscle to back up Harken's mouth.</p>
<p>You're right, it's more likely that they would just gas the chamber. However, it's because of that Kramer did what she did. They're functioning and attacking in ways well outside standard operating procedures for Foundation Agents, so that the groups attacked won't immediately think The Foundation did it.</p>
<p>I'm hoping to dive a bit more in the the characters themselves in coming stories, and hopefully round things out a bit more&#8230;</p>

							</div>

								
					
